# ops/gates/logs/ - scrubbed battery output, one file per exit assertion.
#
# Naming: <ID>.<sha8>.log, written by tools/gate.sh
#   (quality/23_PHASE_GATES.md section 4, the ledger tree).
#
# These files are COMMITTED. They are scrubbed by tools/scrub.py before they are
# written, and CI runs `gitleaks detect --source ops/gates` on every push
# (section 2.2). A gate log that fails the scan blocks the merge, and the secret
# it exposed is rotated before anything else happens.
#
# This file exists so the directory survives a clone while it is empty. Do not
# delete it when the first log lands.
#
# Reading the directory:
#   head -1 ops/gates/logs/*.log        every header at a glance
#   grep -L 'exit=0' ops/gates/logs/*.log   exactly the assertions that failed
